WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.722
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:16.308
Unit seven: Countable and Uncountable Nouns. Today you will use some, any, much, many, a lot of and a few or a little.

4
00:00:16.608 --> 00:00:19.225
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.585
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.370
Countable.

7
00:00:26.383 --> 00:00:28.174
Countable means can be counted.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:30.214
Apples are countable.

9
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:33.225
Your turn. Say: Countable.

10
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:37.079
Countable.

11
00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:39.004
Uncountable.

12
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:42.399
Uncountable means cannot be counted.

13
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:44.460
Water is uncountable.

14
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.540
Your turn. Say: Uncountable.

15
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.494
Uncountable.

16
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.205
Quantity.

17
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:56.518
Quantity means an amount of something.

18
00:00:57.117 --> 00:00:58.954
A large quantity of rice.

19
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.226
Your turn. Say: Quantity.

20
00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:05.952
Quantity.

21
00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:07.544
Many.

22
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.689
Many means a large number of (countable).

23
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:12.424
How many books?

24
00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:15.089
Your turn. Say: Many.

25
00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:18.749
Many.

26
00:01:19.483 --> 00:01:20.484
Much.

27
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:23.889
Much means a large amount of (uncountable).

28
00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:25.612
How much water?

29
00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:28.439
Your turn. Say: Much.

30
00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:31.964
Much.

31
00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:33.660
A few.

32
00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.917
A few means a small number (countable).

33
00:01:37.517 --> 00:01:39.145
I have a few friends.

34
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.228
Your turn. Say: A few.

35
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.056
A few.

36
00:01:46.817 --> 00:01:47.481
A little.

37
00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:50.924
A little means a small amount (uncountable).

38
00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:52.936
I need a little time.

39
00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.784
Your turn. Say: A little.

40
00:01:58.633 --> 00:01:59.507
A little.

41
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.019
Piece of.

42
00:02:02.017 --> 00:02:04.597
Piece of means a unit for uncountable nouns.

43
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:06.672
A piece of advice.

44
00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:09.611
Your turn. Say: Piece of.

45
00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:13.247
Piece of.

46
00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.765
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.617 --> 00:02:22.242
Visal, what is the difference between countable and uncountable nouns?

48
00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:34.036
Countable nouns have a plural, for example one book and two books. Uncountable nouns have no plural, such as water, rice, advice and information.

49
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.975
Which quantifiers do we use?

50
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:47.240
With countable nouns we use many and a few. With uncountable nouns we use much and a little. We use a lot of with both, and some and any with both.

51
00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.827
What about some and any?

52
00:02:50.917 --> 00:03:00.294
We use some in positive sentences and any in negatives and questions: I have some rice. I don't have any money. Do you have any questions?

53
00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:03.328
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:09.352
Grammar focus: Countable: many, a few; uncountable: much, a little.

55
00:03:09.652 --> 00:03:10.897
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.583 --> 00:03:13.455
How many books do you have?

57
00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.466
How much water do you drink every day?

58
00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:23.463
Use many and a few with countable nouns, much and a little with uncountable nouns, and a lot of with both.

59
00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:27.229
Be careful! Don't say: I don't have many water.

60
00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.282
Say: I don't have much water.

61
00:03:31.582 --> 00:03:33.245
Water is uncountable.

62
00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:36.929
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:38.839
At the Market.

64
00:03:39.139 --> 00:03:42.172
Maly buys some rice, a few eggs and a little salt.

65
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:44.806
She does not need much sugar.

66
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.659
The seller asks how many mangoes she wants.

67
00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:52.444
She says a few, because she doesn't have much money.

68
00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.317
She carries a lot of bags home.

69
00:03:56.433 --> 00:04:00.377
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:01.217 --> 00:04:02.972
How blank eggs do you need?

71
00:04:03.272 --> 00:04:06.450
A, a little. B, many. C, much.

72
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.092
The answer is B: many.

73
00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.727
I don't have blank money.

74
00:04:15.027 --> 00:04:18.263
A, many. B, a few. C, much.

75
00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.533
The answer is C: much.

76
00:04:24.683 --> 00:04:26.393
Which noun is uncountable?

77
00:04:26.693 --> 00:04:29.464
A, rice. B, egg. C, book.

78
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.499
The answer is A: rice.

79
00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.313
Maly buys a blank salt.

80
00:04:38.613 --> 00:04:41.767
A, many. B, little. C, few.

81
00:04:45.333 --> 00:04:47.054
The answer is B: little.

82
00:04:48.217 --> 00:04:49.671
'Any' is used in blank.

83
00:04:49.971 --> 00:04:55.087
A, only positives. B, only numbers. C, negatives and questions.

84
00:04:58.633 --> 00:05:01.190
The answer is C: negatives and questions.

85
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.772
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:06.617 --> 00:05:08.396
What food do you have at home?

87
00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.788
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:19.088 --> 00:05:29.185
At home we have a lot of rice and a few eggs. We have some vegetables, but we don't have much fruit today. My mother needs a little sugar for the soup.

89
00:05:29.485 --> 00:05:31.171
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:32.083 --> 00:05:39.310
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and countable: many, a few; uncountable: much, a little.

91
00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:43.435
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

92
00:05:43.735 --> 00:05:46.039
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

93
00:05:46.339 --> 00:05:48.666
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

